  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO/ARM: Tegeta Sustainability-Linked Transport Bond Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tegeta will issue amortizing 5-year sustainability-linked bonds (SLBs) with a weighted average life of four years, to be listed on the Georgian Stock Exchange (GSE) in the first half of December 2025. This will be the first SLBs in lari, and the first in the transport sector in the Caucasus. The mandate of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to act as strategic investor, sustainability coordinator, and mobilizing agent will support the issuance of this landmark transaction and attract private investors. The commitments under the SLBs will help reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions across the group and will further contribute to Georgia&apos;s commitment to the Paris Agreement of reducing GHG emissions by 35% and Armenia&apos;s targets of reduction by 40% below 1990 levels.</narrative>
  </description>
